research/audit/wave7-proof-contracts.json:24437:        "notes": "critical risk (9): 8 declared dependencies; 5 cited facts; boundary-sensitive language; induction, recursion, or minimality, routed by risk-report.mjs. The read-only DeepSeek V4 Pro audit-refuter received the complete target and every cited dependency and returned CLEAN. Boundary evidence: The n=0 case (empty family) is handled by defining the minimum as the constant‑1 map, which is continuous and matches the lattice convention (top element). The n=1 case reduces to the given f_0. Endpoint behaviour of [0,1] is covered because the subspace basis consists of sets (a,b)∩[0,1]; the preimage calculation for m works for all real a,b and correctly restricts to the domain [0,1]^2. The induction base (n=0,1) and step (n→n+1) are valid, so every finite n is reached. Degenerate cases where a≥b give empty preimages, open by definition. No counterexample was found; the claim holds for every topological space X. Checked surface: Title, Statement, Facts & Assumptions, every numbered proof step (1.1, 1.2, 2.1, 3.1), and Remarks (none present) were read. ``` Alpha adjudicated the return against the current item and cited dependencies on disk and found no fatal mathematical or dependency-citation defect. Evidence: research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/lem-finite-minima-of-continuous-unit-interval-maps--ce6751bc06467933.result.json."
